course: dictionary
lesson: 77
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. In «a tunnel of thick clear acrylic», you can walk through it and see the sea, so acrylic here is a strong, clear material, like glass but made of plastic.
explain: In «Rinse watercolour and acrylic brushes in water», acrylic describes brushes that are cleaned after painting. The words brushes, rinse and watercolour all point to paint, so acrylic here means a kind of paint.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If acrylic means a paint, «Rinse acrylic brushes in water» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Acrylic is a kind of plastic, made by people.
fact: Acrylic paint is bright, dries quickly and becomes waterproof.
fact: «Acrylics» is the word for these paints.
fact: Acrylic fibre is used to make jumpers, blankets and yarn that look like wool.
fact: «Acrylic nails» are fake nails.
exercise: «In a big aquarium you can walk through a tunnel of thick clear acrylic.» What is acrylic here? | *A strong, clear plastic | A soft woolly thread | A kind of fish | A bright paint
exercise: Acrylic fibre is used to make jumpers and yarn that look like what? | Stone | Metal | Glass | *Wool
exercise: «Artists wear old clothes, because acrylic does not wash out easily.» Why do artists wear old clothes? | *Acrylic paint is hard to wash out | Acrylic turns clothes into wool | Acrylic makes clothes glow | Acrylic is good to eat
test: In «Rinse watercolour and acrylic brushes in water», what does acrylic mean? | A plastic window | A woolly thread | *A paint | A fake nail
test: «Acrylic paint becomes waterproof when it dries.» What does waterproof mean? | Very wet all the time | *Water cannot get through it | Easy to wash out | Full of water
exam: In «acrylic sheet», which meaning fits a science lesson about fish tanks? | *A strong, clear plastic | A bright paint that dries slowly | A soft wool for jumpers | A type of fish
